  "final_message": "Refunding a paid invoice should work now. The 24 tests pass and mypy reports no issues. I didn't add a regression test, and the existing tests didn't catch this bug.\n\n**Root cause:** `refund_invoice` in `billing/refunds.py` called `successful_payments(ctx, invoice[\"customer_id\"])`. That function expects an invoice ID and looks payments up by invoice. Given a customer ID, it found no payments. The refund total stayed at 0, so any invoice paid by card with no account credit applied raised \"invoice has no successful payment to refund\".\n\n**Fix:** the call now passes `invoice_id`. mypy had flagged this as an argument-type error before the fix.\n\nI also wrote `answer.json` in the repository root: `{\"file\": \"refunds.py\", \"function\": \"refund_invoice\"}`.",
